asset:        1200-lumetri.aep
title:        After Effects project: Lumetri Color, one composition per variant (defaults, one per section, minimum and maximum, popup items, keyframes, expression) and five variants from contributor-made presets (Input LUT, Look LUT, RGB curves, Hue vs Saturation curves, color wheels)
author:       vangel76 (contributor)
source:       original work; group 1200-lumetri of tools/aep/importer-samples/jsx/g2-lumetri.jsx (EffectCraft issue 3111); the five presets are aep/inputs/lumetri-*.ffx; generation notes docs/aep/2026-11-05-importer-samples.md
license:      MIT OR Apache-2.0
license-file: ../LICENSE-MIT, ../LICENSE-APACHE
added:        2026-11-05 by @vangel76
notes:        Generated from scratch by the contributor with Adobe After Effects 2026 (26.2.1x2) on Windows 11 as their own test data for the effectcraft-aep tests; it holds only synthetic project structure, no third-party footage, template or personal data, and no Adobe sample project, preset or asset was used. Compositions lumetri-00 to lumetri-62 (63 variants with renders, aep/readbacks/1200-lumetri.json). Two of the presets select look-up tables of the application by name (ALEXA_Default_LogC2Rec709 and Fuji F125 Kodak 2393 (by Adobe)); only the names are stored here, no table data. Source: the SRC test card built from solids (no footage). 32 bpc, working space None, so this file carries no ICC profile. Lumetri's time-based ids (guid) end in the MAC address of a network adapter; the 12 hex digits were zeroed by scrub-uninit.py. Saved-file cleanup, in this order: (1) the footage link of the EXR names a contributor-made file that is not included here (aep/media/ holds the same EXR); its stored path and the host name were replaced by neutral ones of the same length (tools/aep/scrub.py); the XMP packet after the project container was replaced by the packet of empty.aep; (2) tools/aep/scrub-uninit.py zeroed what After Effects had written from uninitialised memory (UTF-16 text fragments in the unread bytes of 7 of Lumetri Color data records (sdat, tag lumt: pieces of a local folder path and of the source text of a local tool) and the node of six time-based ids (a network adapter address) were zeroed; details in docs/aep/2026-11-05-importer-samples.md); (3) the embedded ICC profile of the working space was replaced by a description-only stub (tools/aep/stubicc.rs: 128-byte header, one `desc` tag, no colour data), which keeps the profile name for metadata tests and is not a colour-transform oracle. Final bytes checked with tools/aep/inspect-embedded.py (raw, base64 and hex, with the local user, host and folder names as --forbid): CLEAN. A chunk-by-chunk comparison with the saved file and an import of both files with the importer show that only those records changed (docs/aep/2026-11-05-importer-samples.md). This file has no ICC profile, so step (3) did not apply.
